AB  - In response to the refined demand for high-resolution remote sensing images (RSIs) in urban andrural environmental planning, an RSI processing and analysis framework that integrates intelligentscientific methods is proposed. This method uses a multi-scale residual network to restore highfrequencydetails in images, improving spatial resolution and visual quality.On this basis, a semanticsegmentation model for boundary aggregation calibration and small object mining is proposed,aiming to improve segmentation accuracy and boundary clarity. When the magnification is 8, theproposed super-resolution reconstruction method has peak signal-to-noise ratios of 28.72 dB and31.82 dB in two common datasets, respectively. The highest structural similarity index is 0.964,effectively restoring high-frequency details of the image. In terms of semantic segmentation, theproposed model achieves an average intersection to union ratio of 92.07%, with only 19.27Mparameters and an inference speed of 52.13 FPS. By planning application cases, the key indicator F1score of this method exceeds 85%. The proposed method strengthens the quality and segmentationaccuracy of RSI, effectively supporting the refined analysis and decision-making requirements forurban and rural environmental planning, and providing a reliable solution for its intelligentdevelopment.
