AB  - To address the challenges of missed detections and false alarms caused by dense arrangements, small object scales, and complex backgrounds in remote sensing imagery, this paper proposes a novel algorithm named EagleEye-DETR. First, the backbone network is optimized by integrating the C2f and Cross-Stage Partial Hierarchical Interaction Attention (CSP_HIA) modules. This integration facilitates the complementary fusion of shallow details and deep semantic information. Specifically, the Global Self-Attention (GSA) mechanism in the CSP_HIA module is employed to model long-range dependencies and global context. It captures inter-channel correlations using global spatial information, thereby preserving semantic information for tiny objects. Subsequently, to mitigate the interference of background noise on feature representation, a Spatial-Channel Attention Block (SCA-Block) is designed. This module adaptively focuses on target regions in the spatial dimension to suppress noise and dynamically reweights key features in the channel dimension, significantly enhancing feature discriminability. Finally, to translate enhanced features into precise coordinates, the Minimum Point Distance Intersection over Union (MPDIoU) loss function is introduced. This loss function simplifies computation and heightens sensitivity to positional deviations, thereby improving both localization accuracy and model convergence speed. Experimental results on the VEDAI dataset demonstrate that EagleEye-DETR achieves improvements of 1.21%, 2.35%, 3.29%, and 2.62% in Precision, Recall, mAP@0.5, and mAP@0.5:0.95, respectively, compared to the RT-DETR baseline. Practically, these gains represent a critical enhancement in the model’s ability to identify small, densely packed targets, effectively mitigating the high rates of missed detections and false alarms common in complex remote sensing scenarios. Furthermore, experiments on the RSOD and LEVIR datasets confirm that the proposed algorithm not only exhibits superior detection performance in scenarios with complex backgrounds and dense small targets but also possesses high robustness and generalization capabilities.
