AB  - Ship detection in synthetic aperture radar (SAR) remote sensing images is a fundamental yet challenging task in the field of earth observation. Deep learning-based detection methods have significantly progressed in this area, particularly in identifying ships from SAR images. However, due to the complex backgrounds and the small size of ship targets in SAR images, ship detection remains highly challenging. To further improve the detection accuracy of ship recognition and positioning in SAR images, this paper constructs an enhanced feature preservation and interaction network (EFPINet). Complex SAR image backgrounds and the resulting loss of object information present major obstacles for accurate detection. To overcome these issues, an orthogonal feature information maintenance (OFIM) module is built in EFPINet. The OFIM module employs both horizontal and vertical convolution operations to preserve object feature information effectively while reducing the loss of target information in neural networks. Then, a cross-stage attention mechanism (CSAM) is proposed by integrating local and global features to enhance small ship detection precision. EFPINet achieves an AP of 72.2% and an AP50 of 98.4% on SSDD, and an AP of 69.0% and an AP50 of 93.0% on HRSID, validating its superior capability in SAR ship detection.
