AB  - In recent years, the fusion network model combining agriculture, Convolutional Neural Networks (CNN), and Transformers has become a research hotspot in hyperspectral image classification. However, these models applied to hyperspectral image classification typically adopt a single branch heterogeneous architecture, which combines the local details of CNN and the global attention mechanism of Transformers through simple cascading. The remaining challenge lies in the extraction of detailed and local features. To address these problems, we propose a Spatial-Spectral Interactive Fusion Pooling Transformer Network for Hyperspectral Image Classification(S2IFPTNet), which can efficiently extract multi-scale spatial-spectral features, accurately model nonlinear feature relationships, and effectively fuse multi-modal features. We design a Spatial-Spectral Matrix Fusion Module, which enables multi-scale spatial-spectral feature extraction and accurately captures the complex dependency structures between variables, thus achieving cross-scale spatial-spectral information fusion. In addition, we design a Pooling Cascaded Attention Fusion Module to hierarchically extract feature information of different scales and receptive fields, while preserving key details and global context, so as to improve the completeness and robustness of feature representation. Extensive experiments are conducted on four public hyperspectral image datasets, and the results show that the proposed Spatial-Spectral Interactive Fusion Pooling Transformer Network outperforms the state-of-the-art classification algorithms
