AB  - Vectorized extraction of agricultural parcels is essential for large-area cropland monitoring and management. Existing approaches either predict raster masks followed by heuristic vectorization or directly regress field contours using dense vertex sequences along the boundary. However, these pipelines often result in limited boundary regularity, redundant polygon vertices, and incomplete reconstruction of parcels that span multiple image patches. To address these issues, we propose the Boundary-to-Polygon Network (B2PNet), a Boundary Line Segment-based (BLS-based) reconstruction pipeline for generating agricultural field polygons. Instead of relying on dense pixel boundaries or vertex-based contour regression, B2PNet represents each parcel as a set of oriented and ordered Boundary Line Segments (BLSs) and predicts their pairwise connectivity to assemble closed polygonal geometries. This representation explicitly encodes structural boundary information, leading to more accurate boundary localization as well as significantly improved polygon regularity and vertex efficiency. To support large-area mapping, we further develop an image-level post-processing strategy that leverages the boundary adherence property of the BLS-based pipeline, ensuring geometric alignment across patch borders and enabling complete reconstruction of parcels that span multiple patches. Extensive experiments on the AI4SmallFarms and iFLYTEK datasets show that B2PNet achieves state-of-the-art performance across both region-level and boundary-level evaluations. On AI4SmallFarms, B2PNet improves the F1-scores for parcel extraction and boundary delineation to 54.39% and 53.54%, respectively, substantially outperforming the strong contour-based baseline E2EVAP (48.91% and 48.78%). Moreover, B2PNet achieves the best polygon regularity (PoLiS, MTA) and vertex efficiency (N ratio, C-IoU), confirming its advantages in geometric fidelity and polygon compactness. Cross-dataset experiments further demonstrate its strong robustness and generalization capability across diverse agricultural regions.
