AB  - This study proposes a segmentation network optimization framework tailored for different types of datasets, based on representative remote sensing building datasets. The framework integrates four representative deep learning methods - PointRend, BCNet, ESFNet, and DeepLabV3+ - covering the current mainstream approaches for building extraction. By two practical application scenarios with typical datasets - data scarcity and data abundance - the study systematically analyzes the performance of various network architectures across different datasets. The performance of different algorithms under diverse scenarios is examined to provide a decision-making reference for building extraction in complex remote sensing image environments.
