AB  - Due to the powerful feature extraction and image processing capabilities of convolutional neural networks, significant attention has been attracted to their use in change detection (CD) tasks. However, existing studies often treat features from changed and unchanged regions as equally important, emphasizing deep features while neglecting more global shallow features, which leaves significant room for improvement in CD performance. We proposed a multi-scale attention ONet (MSF-ONet) to enhance the accuracy of CD tasks by extracting and learning input feature maps of dual-temporal hyperspectral images (HSIs) at different scales. Specifically, an ONet backbone integrated with squeeze-and-excitation networks (SE) inception and attention in skip line modules is first constructed to extract and learn features from dual-temporal HSIs. A difference feature map fusion module is then built to combine differential features across scales, and a multi-scale convolutional attention for change detection module is designed for more efficient deep information mining. Extensive experiments demonstrate that the proposed MSF-ONet outperforms existing state-of-the-art methods on three popular HSI CD datasets.
