AB  - In this work, a physics informed deep learning methodology has been proposed for automated hazard mapping using the multimodal satellite data. The proposed system features large scale GeoTIFF preprocessing, tiled data extraction, metadata preservation, a UNet-based encoder-decoder architecture, partial differential equation-based loss regularization, mixed precision training, and GPU-optimized streaming inference. Experiments show that the tile based inference performance in real-time is 42.9 tiles/s, which makes it operationally viable for early hazard detection applications: it took around 1.10 minutes for 2839 tiles.
