AB  - In various stages of agriculture such as crop management, improve yield and reduce environmental impact. Integrating heterogeneous datasets such as satellite imagery, UAV data, soil properties, IoT sensor readings, and historical crop records can enhance decision-making in farming. This research proposes a comprehensive AI pipeline that fuses these multimodal datasets to deliver actionable insights in real-time. The pipeline encompasses data ingestion, pre- processing, feature extraction, predictive modelling, and decision support. Deep learning models handle image-based anomaly detection, while classical machine learning (Random Forest, Gradient Boosting) predicts yield, water, and nutrient requirements. The system incorporates explainable AI techniques to ensure interpretability and reliability of recommendations. Validation on multimodal datasets demonstrates the pipeline's effectiveness in improving crop productivity and predicting the yield. This framework provides a scalable and adaptable solution for smart farming systems, making way for sustainable and data-driven agricultural systems.
