AB  - Big data has transformed economic crisis detection by analyzing vast datasets from financial markets, macroeconomic indicators, and alternative sources like satellite imagery and social media sentiment. The surge in global financial transactions, reaching $12.6 trillion daily in 2023, underscores the need for real- time analysis. Traditional forecasting models (ARIMA, VAR, GARCH) often fail to capture nonlinear trends and disruptions. Machine learning (ML) and AI models, including RNN, LSTM, and transformers, enhance predictive accuracy by detecting financial anomalies. AI- driven models, such as deep learning- based credit risk analysis, have improved prediction accuracy by up to 30%. Economic indicators like GDP contraction, inflation volatility, and VIX index trends aid crisis detection. NLP- based sentiment analysis of financial news further enhances predictions. Challenges persist in data privacy and regulatory compliance, but advancements in distributed computing and ethical AI will strengthen economic forecasting and crisis mitigation.
