AB  - The main purpose of this article is to develop an efficient prediction model of tobacco purity by combining hyperspectral imaging (HSI) technology and machine learning (ML). In this study, the detailed spectral information of tobacco samples was obtained by HSI technology, and the data quality was optimized through pretreatment and feature extraction. Then, the convolutional neural network (CNN) is used to deeply learn these data, automatically extract features and build a classification model. The results show that the accuracy, recall and F1 value of this model reach 95%, 93% and 93.1% respectively, which is significantly better than traditional algorithms such as support vector machine (SVM) and decision tree (DT). The response time of the system is only 5 seconds, which greatly improves the detection efficiency. In one month's actual production line test, 720 tobacco samples can be detected every hour, and the detection failure rate is as low as 0.5%. The research shows that the method based on the combination of HSI and CNN improves the speed and accuracy of tobacco purity detection and provides a new solution for the quality control of tobacco industry.
