AB  - The mining industry is being reshaped by Artificial Intelligence (AI), the Internet of Things (IoT), and Remote Sensing. Traditional monitoring often operates in silos, limiting integration of satellite imagery, sensor data, and geospatial metadata. To address this, we propose the Cognitive Knowledge Framework (CKF), a modular system unifying multimodal data for smart mining. CKF includes four agents: the Vision Agent (detects changes in satellite images using models such as U- Net and ChangeFFT U- Net), the Sensor Agent (monitors vibration, dust, and temperature via IoT), the Geo Agent (provides geo- spatial intelligence and mapping), and the Intent Interpreter (enables natural language queries). Results show ChangeFFT U- Net improves segmentation, especially for subtle mining- induced changes. CKF also integrates digital twin concepts with real- time monitoring, offering insights for sustainable mining, environmental monitoring, and risk management. This research advances Mining 4.0 by showing how multimodal fusion supports safer, more efficient, and sustainable mining.
